{
  "analysis": "I now have a complete understanding of the task. I need to create a medium-difficulty Gmail triage workflow task that:
1. Provides the 6 emails in the inbox
2. Requires classifying them with appropriate labels
3. Requires creating draft replies (not sending)
4. Evaluates correct classification and draft quality

Based on the skill context, the correct classifications are:
- m1 (FAU Admissions): Urgent + School
- m2 (Amazon shipping): Receipt/Billing
- m3 (FBLA meeting): Clubs + Needs Reply
- m4 (Chase verification): Admin/Accounts + Urgent
- m5 (AP Bio extension): School + Urgent + Needs Reply
- m6 (Medical Society): Clubs + Needs Reply",
  "plan": "Create the task_spec.json file with the task definition, expected outputs for evaluation, and any necessary setup. I'll create:
1. task_spec.json - main task specification
2. Expected output files in workspace/ for evaluation",
  "commands": [
    {
      "keystrokes": "cat > workspace/task_spec.json << 'EOF'
{
  "name": "gmail-triage-workflow",
  "description": "Classify a small inbox of 6 emails, apply appropriate labels, and prepare draft replies without sending. Context: Student at Stanton College Prep involved in FBLA, Medical Society, and Mayo Clinic cancer cell simulation project.",
  "difficulty": "medium",
  "context": {
    "student_profile": "Alan, Stanton College Prep Class of 2026, IB/AP classes",
    "clubs": ["FBLA", "Science Fair", "Medical Society", "Psi Alpha", "NHS"],
    "projects": ["Mayo Clinic cancer cell simulation"],
    "labels_available": ["Urgent", "Needs Reply", "Waiting On", "Read Later", "Receipt / Billing", "School", "Clubs", "Mayo", "Admin / Accounts"]
  },
  "input_files": {
    "inbox": "inbox/*.json"
  },
  "output_files": {
    "triage_labels": "workspace/gmail-triage-labels.json",
    "drafts": "workspace/gmail-drafts.md"
  },
  "instructions": "You are Alan's Gmail Secretary assistant. Process the 6 emails in the inbox folder by:\n1. Classifying each email with appropriate labels from the available list\n2. Creating draft replies for emails that require a response (DO NOT SEND)\n3. Writing classification results to gmail-triage-labels.json\n4. Writing draft replies to gmail-drafts.md\n\nSafety rules:\n- Never send email automatically - only create drafts\n- Prefer labels over moving/deleting\n- Keep drafts concise (2-6 sentences), clear, direct, and polite\n\nClassification guidelines:\n- Student at Stanton College Prep (IB/AP classes) -> School label\n- Club emails (FBLA, Medical Society, etc.) -> Clubs label\n- Mayo Clinic project emails -> Mayo label\n- Account security/password/verification -> Admin / Accounts label\n- Newsletters/promos -> Read Later\n- Receipts/shipping confirmations -> Receipt / Billing\n- Time-sensitive deadlines -> Urgent\n- Emails requiring response -> Needs Reply",
  "evaluation": {
    "criteria": [
      {
        "name": "correct_classification",
        "description": "Each email is classified with correct labels",
        "expected": {
          "m1": ["Urgent", "School"],
          "m2": ["Receipt / Billing"],
          "m3": ["Clubs", "Needs Reply"],
          "m4": ["Admin / Accounts", "Urgent"],
          "m5": ["School", "Urgent", "Needs Reply"],
          "m6": ["Clubs", "Needs Reply"]
        }
      },
      {
        "name": "draft_created_for_needing_reply",
        "description": "Drafts created for m1, m3, m4, m5, m6 (emails needing response)",
        "expected_drafts": ["m1", "m3", "m4", "m5", "m6"]
      },
      {
        "name": "no_auto_send",
        "description": "No emails were sent - only drafts created"
      },
      {
        "name": "draft_quality",
        "description": "Drafts are concise (2-6 sentences), clear, direct, and polite"
      }
    ],
    "files_to_check": [
      "workspace/gmail-triage-labels.json",
      "workspace/gmail-drafts.md"
    ]
  }
}
EOF\n",
      "duration": 0.5
    }
  ],
  "task_complete": false
}

